[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-identity.cxd — the identity repository's page,
   repo-cx-platform-identity.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 2).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the
   session suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-identity
  [intro
    """Who is asking, as a value. `cx-platform-identity` turns a
       verified token into a session bound to a principal and a tenant,
       maps claims to that principal deterministically, resolves `did:web`
       identifiers, keeps authorization rows in the store and answers
       whether a credential has been revoked."""]
  [body
    """A session is attached from a token checked against the issuer's keys,
       and every question about it is answered as a value: an unattached
       request, an unknown session id, an unknown client are all absence you
       can ask about with `[?else]`, never an exception. The claim mapping is
       pure — the same claims map to the same principal every time — so a
       policy written against a principal can be tested without a token in
       hand."""]
  [body
    """The rest of the repository is the identity fabric around the session:
       `did:web` resolution refuses to reach the network until it is granted
       and refuses a self-describing document; the authorization store keeps
       grants as rows the engine can query and replay; credential revocation
       is an append to a journal and a fold over one — a fact that outlives
       the process and is visible to a second party. The single sign-on
       protocols themselves live one repository over, in the sso module."""]
  [gives
    """Four modules of the platform group: the session layer, the
       authorization store, `did:web` resolution and credential revocation.
       Each links to its reference page, projected from the module's own
       documentation."""]
  [try
    """A claims document mapped to a principal with no session in hand — the
       tenant from `tid`, the identity from `sub`, and the same answer every
       time it is asked."""]
  [fixture id=session-005-map-claims-pure]
  [status
    """The identity repository builds on the store, the wire and the session
       layer, and the application host builds on it; the front door compiles
       its V module from the pin."""]]
